- Green (N) timer\n- Light gray (w) bottom bar\nWhat if the goal is to make all objects the same color? Or to change the blue bar's color to match something?\nOr what if the goal is to \"paint\" the blue bar onto the charcoal/magenta block by moving it there and pressing SPACE?\nLet me try one more thing: move the blue bar to be directly below the charcoal+magenta block (matching left edges at col 36), then press SPACE.\nFrom cols 20-39, I need RIGHT 4 times to get to cols 36-55.", "kind": "reasoning", "inContext": false}, {"label": "TOOL CALL: python", "content": "<tool_call>\n<function=python>\n<parameter=code>\n# Timer at 53, running low\n# Blue bar at rows 16-19, cols 20-39\n# Charcoal+magenta at rows 1-7, cols 36-39\n# Try aligning blue bar left edge with charcoal+magenta left edge (col 36)\n# RIGHT 4: 20->24->28->32->36, blue bar at cols 36-55\n# Then SPACE\n\nresult = action(['RIGHT', 'RIGHT', 'RIGHT', 'RIGHT', 'SPACE'])\nseg = current_frame.segmentation\nfor n in seg['nodes']:\n    boundary = n['boundary']\n    if boundary:\n        rows = [p[0] for p in boundary]\n        cols = [p[1] for p in boundary]\n        rmin, rmax = min(rows), max(rows)\n        cmin, cmax = min(cols), max(cols)\n        if n['color'] in ['b', 'Y', 'c', 'M', 'N', 'w']:\n            print(f\"  color={n['color']} rows={rmin}-{rmax} cols={cmin}-{cmax} px={n['pixels']}\")\nprint(f\"Game over: {result.get('game_over')}\")\nprint(f\"Level completed: {result.get('level_completed')}\")\nprint(f\"Done: {result.get('done')}\")\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}, {"label": "TOOL RESULT: python", "content": "color=N rows=0-0 cols=0-42 px=43\n  color=c rows=1-3 cols=36-39 px=12\n  color=M rows=4-7 cols=36-39 px=16\n  color=b rows=16-19 cols=36-55 px=80\n  color=Y rows=52-59 cols=16-27 px=80\n  color=Y rows=52-59 cols=40-51 px=80\n  color=w rows=60-63 cols=0-63 px=256\nGame over: False\nLevel completed: False\nDone: False", "kind": "tool", "inContext": 